<title>USA: Air Wisconsin Feb. load factor rises to 58.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Air Wisconsin Feb. load factor rises to 58.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>APPLETON, Wis. 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Wisconsin Airlines Corp said its passenger load factor last month rose to 58.9 percent from 45.1 percent in February of 1996.</p>
<p>The carrier, operating as United Express, said its available seat miles fell to 76,692 from 79,674, while its revenue passenger miles rose to 45,168 from 35,921.</p>
<p>Air Wisconsin operates 15 jets as United Express feeding the Chicago and Denver hubs of UAL Corp subsidiary United Airlines.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
